        "title": "Masonry - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Masonry is the art and engineering of building with discrete units bonded by mortar (or dry-stacked). The defining structural constraint — units strong in compression, negligible in tension — drives every design decision from arch geometry to buttress placement to reinforcement strategy."
    },
