        "title": "Masonry - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Masonry units are strong in compression (brick: 3,000–20,000 psi), negligible in tension (<100 psi). Mortar joints are the weakest link in tension. This single fact drives the entire history of the discipline."
